description:
List top pages of a property ranked by a chosen metric with period-over-period comparison. Accepts a date range as presets (last_7_days, last_28_days, last_3_months, last_year) or as absolute dates (from/to in Y-m-d format). Sort by clicks, impressions, position, or ctr. Returns all four metrics per page (clicks, impressions, ctr, position — each with current value, previous-period value, diff, and change_pct) and cursor pagination. Optional filters: country (ISO-3166 alpha-3, e.g. "usa"), device ("desktop"/"mobile"/"tablet"), position_min/position_max to keep only pages whose current-period average position falls in that range (applied regardless of sort, not combinable with country/device yet), tags (array of page tag names from list_tags — keeps only pages carrying any of those tags), and url_contains (case-insensitive text matched anywhere in the URL, same as the search box of the Pages report; a plain substring, so "hasta-5000" also matches "hasta-50000"). With url_contains the response adds "summary" with total_urls, clicks and impressions for every matching page in the period (not only the returned page), so one call sizes a URL segment; no match returns an empty list and zero totals. url_contains may also be a list of up to 1000 texts (batch): the response then carries "url_contains_totals" — total_urls, clicks, impressions, ctr and impression-weighted position per text, in the order of the input — plus "summary" with the overall total over pages matching at least one text (each page counted once); a batch call returns no page list ("pages" is empty) and no cursor, and rejects a cursor. Position is returned on every row. The applied filters are echoed back under "filters". Pass the property ID (UUID) or URL (sc-domain:...) from list_properties.

Cost: 5 credits per call.

Examples:
```json
// Top 25 pages by clicks over the last 28 days.
{"property":"sc-domain:example.com","range":"last_28_days","sortBy":"clicks","limit":25}

// Total URLs, clicks and impressions of every /blog/ URL (summary), plus its top 10 pages.
{"property":"sc-domain:example.com","from":"2026-08-01","to":"2026-10-31","urlContains":"/blog/","limit":10}

// Batch: clicks, impressions, ctr and position of each price band in one call (url_contains_totals, same order as the input), plus the overall total (summary).
{"property":"sc-domain:example.com","from":"2026-08-01","to":"2026-10-31","urlContains":["/price-100-200/","/price-200-300/","/price-300-400/"]}
```
